WEBVTT
Kind: captions

00:00:48.448 --> 00:00:49.936 position:63%
[blues music]

00:00:54.021 --> 00:00:56.189 position:63%
[Peter] All right, guys,
this is the town of Winthrop.

00:00:56.256 --> 00:01:00.527 position:63%
And I think this is the only
tourist town we're gonna see today.

00:01:00.594 --> 00:01:03.463 position:63%
You can see the old western facades here.

00:01:03.530 --> 00:01:05.499 position:63%
Cool old downtown.

00:01:05.566 --> 00:01:08.702 position:63%
Since we got an ambitious
get out into the countryside journey,

00:01:08.769 --> 00:01:11.571 position:63%
I don't want to spend too much time here.

00:01:11.644 --> 00:01:13.740 position:63%
But it's basically come over
the Cascade Mountains.

00:01:13.807 --> 00:01:16.910 position:63%
On the other side
of Washington is very green.

00:01:16.977 --> 00:01:20.313 position:63%
And that's where
most of the precipitation drops.

00:01:20.380 --> 00:01:22.949 position:63%
And then we're starting to
step into rain shadow land.

00:01:23.016 --> 00:01:27.087 position:63%
And so I would say we're
sort of in a high desert right now.

00:01:27.154 --> 00:01:28.801 position:63%
This is a cute little town. It's nice.

00:01:28.868 --> 00:01:34.127 position:63%
You can see there's probably
some pandemic migration here.

00:01:34.194 --> 00:01:39.099 position:63%
Like so much of the West or really
any part of the country that's nice.

00:01:39.166 --> 00:01:42.769 position:63%
Look at the deer here.
They just come right up to the homes.

00:01:42.836 --> 00:01:43.879 position:63%
Not bashful.

00:01:45.005 --> 00:01:49.342 position:63%
And we'll check out this setup
really quickly before we hit the road.

00:01:53.308 --> 00:01:56.857 position:63%
Oh yeah, that smell of pine in the air.

00:01:57.852 --> 00:02:01.922 position:63%
Looks like we have
an old pioneering museum of sorts.

00:02:02.389 --> 00:02:08.210 position:63%
And you can see not long ago, these towns
were built off of mining and logging.

00:02:09.228 --> 00:02:13.066 position:63%
You have the old trading company.
The general store was everything.

00:02:13.133 --> 00:02:15.962 position:63%
As it says here, the heart of any town.

00:02:16.029 --> 00:02:17.342 position:63%
This was the trading post.

00:02:17.409 --> 00:02:20.276 position:63%
People would come in
from around the region.

00:02:20.807 --> 00:02:24.354 position:63%
Maybe working a claim.
Maybe tilling a field.

00:02:25.079 --> 00:02:27.411 position:63%
Coming in to the center of town.

00:02:28.081 --> 00:02:33.112 position:63%
And look at the construction back then.
Just these beautiful log buildings.

00:02:33.654 --> 00:02:35.755 position:63%
Little schoolhouse, that's what it is.

00:02:35.822 --> 00:02:39.192 position:63%
Even in hard times,
settlers regarded school as essential.

00:02:39.259 --> 00:02:40.961 position:63%
They held classes in homes.

00:02:41.028 --> 00:02:42.963 position:63%
Then built small schools
up and down the valley

00:02:43.030 --> 00:02:45.632 position:63%
with donated land, timber and labor.

00:02:45.699 --> 00:02:50.557 position:63%
At least 24 schools
were built between 1890 and 1940.

00:02:51.672 --> 00:02:52.806 position:63%
Okay, terms were short.

00:02:52.873 --> 00:02:56.409 position:63%
School was called off when snow was
too deep or summer farm work intervened.

00:02:56.476 --> 00:02:58.411 position:63%
Schoolhouses rarely stood empty.

00:02:58.478 --> 00:03:00.413 position:63%
They were a place for church services,

00:03:00.480 --> 00:03:03.683 position:63%
card games,
town meetings and lively dance parties.

00:03:03.750 --> 00:03:05.452 position:63%
I guess it was apples here.

00:03:05.519 --> 00:03:08.723 position:63%
And when that froze out,
they had to figure out something.

00:03:08.790 --> 00:03:11.146 position:63%
So a lot of history here.

00:03:11.973 --> 00:03:14.640 position:63%
And they did a great job with this zone.

00:03:15.262 --> 00:03:16.892 position:63%
Carriages over here.

00:03:17.330 --> 00:03:21.906 position:63%
The press put the news out
to the local residents.

00:03:22.715 --> 00:03:23.937 position:63%
Really quite awesome.

00:03:24.004 --> 00:03:25.471 position:63%
The saloon, of course.

00:03:26.432 --> 00:03:30.075 position:63%
You can see the carts
getting the minerals out of the mountains.

00:03:30.143 --> 00:03:33.951 position:63%
And all this machinery
built up the region,

00:03:34.010 --> 00:03:37.289 position:63%
the country,
and made the West what it is today.

00:03:37.365 --> 00:03:38.877 position:63%
[blues music]

00:03:57.313 --> 00:03:59.846 position:63%
All right, here we have downtown Omak.

00:04:00.807 --> 00:04:04.544 position:63%
Came over that mountain pass,
through the apple orchards.

00:04:04.611 --> 00:04:07.897 position:63%
A lot of agriculture,
you can tell by the trucks

00:04:07.964 --> 00:04:09.998 position:63%
and the fields coming into town.

00:04:10.065 --> 00:04:15.622 position:63%
And the Colville Indian Reservation's
across the river.

00:04:16.102 --> 00:04:19.192 position:63%
And you're in a different world
to some degree.

00:04:19.259 --> 00:04:21.928 position:63%
Now this tribe is huge,
as in the landmass.

00:04:21.995 --> 00:04:24.731 position:63%
There are very few people living out here.

00:04:24.798 --> 00:04:28.968 position:63%
And it's actually
12 different tribes on Colville.

00:04:29.035 --> 00:04:30.771 position:63%
They got a nice park.

00:04:30.838 --> 00:04:33.206 position:63%
Big stadium in the distance.

00:04:33.273 --> 00:04:35.341 position:63%
The reason there are
12 tribes here is because

00:04:35.408 --> 00:04:38.745 position:63%
when the US was putting
Natives on reservations,

00:04:38.812 --> 00:04:41.581 position:63%
they basically took tribes
from the surrounding areas

00:04:41.648 --> 00:04:44.974 position:63%
and put them all
on this one chunk of land here.

00:04:45.585 --> 00:04:48.138 position:63%
Looks like the house burnt down.

00:04:48.821 --> 00:04:50.954 position:63%
A bit rough back in these areas.

00:04:51.491 --> 00:04:55.729 position:63%
Different reality than Winthrop
where we started this morning.

00:04:55.796 --> 00:04:56.863 position:63%
That's for sure.

00:05:01.367 --> 00:05:03.672 position:63%
You can see their flag, Colville.

00:05:06.140 --> 00:05:07.746 position:63%
Confederated Tribes.

00:05:09.910 --> 00:05:11.411 position:63%
So we're right here.

00:05:11.478 --> 00:05:12.811 position:63%
We started off here.

00:05:13.513 --> 00:05:18.084 position:63%
And gonna go all the way up
right near the Canadian border today.

00:05:18.151 --> 00:05:19.910 position:63%
Get over to Chesaw.

00:05:19.977 --> 00:05:23.752 position:63%
And then make our way
down to Wauconda and over.

00:05:24.658 --> 00:05:26.498 position:63%
Almost to the Idaho border.

00:05:27.260 --> 00:05:30.016 position:63%
The area now known as Omak
was originally inhabited by

00:05:30.083 --> 00:05:34.073 position:63%
various Native American tribes
before non-Indigenous settlers arrived

00:05:34.140 --> 00:05:35.748 position:63%
in the early 19th century.

00:05:35.815 --> 00:05:39.539 position:63%
The name Omak is derived from
the Okanagan place name.

00:05:39.630 --> 00:05:41.742 position:63%
Or the Salishan term, Omache.

00:05:41.809 --> 00:05:44.997 position:63%
Which means good medicine or plenty.

00:05:48.048 --> 00:05:53.494 position:63%
[man] I grew up just across the river,
but a lot of my family grew up on the res.

00:05:53.561 --> 00:05:57.056 position:63%
-So you're part Native?
-Yeah, yeah. I'm technically a descendant.

00:05:57.123 --> 00:05:59.060 position:63%
-What's it like out here these days?

00:05:59.127 --> 00:06:01.600 position:63%
Uh… Small town life.

00:06:02.162 --> 00:06:04.731 position:63%
Not a lot of job opportunities.

00:06:04.798 --> 00:06:10.070 position:63%
Most people have to either travel for work
or work remotely.

00:06:10.137 --> 00:06:13.173 position:63%
-Okay, so how was your family
growing up on the res?

00:06:13.240 --> 00:06:16.911 position:63%
Is it much different growing up on the res
than over the river here?

00:06:16.978 --> 00:06:22.448 position:63%
Yeah, yeah.
In my opinion, Native Americans now,

00:06:22.515 --> 00:06:24.851 position:63%
especially ones that live
on the reservation,

00:06:24.918 --> 00:06:30.500 position:63%
are reliant on the tribe
and the government to live.

00:06:31.057 --> 00:06:35.228 position:63%
They don't really have a lot of motivation
to go and do better for themselves.

00:06:35.295 --> 00:06:40.166 position:63%
They gotta just wait for the handouts that
come from the tribe and the government.

00:06:40.233 --> 00:06:42.001 position:63%
-Across the river, you don't get that?

00:06:42.068 --> 00:06:46.406 position:63%
No, because it's not a thing.
You have to work to live.

00:06:46.473 --> 00:06:49.551 position:63%
-If you grow up here and you're motivated,
you probably get out, right?

00:06:49.618 --> 00:06:51.511 position:63%
Yep. Yep. Exactly.

00:06:51.578 --> 00:06:55.372 position:63%
-Do you know how much Native you are?
-Uh, like a sixteenth I think.

00:06:55.439 --> 00:06:58.618 position:63%
-What's the blood quantum they allow
for being Native here?

00:06:58.691 --> 00:07:00.420 position:63%
-A quarter.
-It's a quarter?

00:07:00.487 --> 00:07:03.456 position:63%
-Can non-Natives live on the res here?
-Yes.

00:07:03.523 --> 00:07:04.791 position:63%
-Okay, that's interesting.

00:07:04.858 --> 00:07:11.631 position:63%
Yeah, there's a thing called fee land,
so they take and the land gets surveyed,

00:07:11.698 --> 00:07:15.501 position:63%
becomes part of the county,
so you have to pay taxes on it.

00:07:15.568 --> 00:07:18.404 position:63%
But Natives don't have to
pay tax on their land.

00:07:18.471 --> 00:07:20.974 position:63%
-Okay, so every res is different.
-Yep.

00:07:21.041 --> 00:07:23.309 position:63%
-Some reses, that's not possible.
-Right.

00:07:23.376 --> 00:07:24.644 position:63%
-But here it is.
-Yep.

00:07:24.711 --> 00:07:27.148 position:63%
Does that create friction here,
do you think?

00:07:27.215 --> 00:07:29.883 position:63%
Uh, sometimes, yeah.

00:07:29.950 --> 00:07:32.018 position:63%
There are some families
that have been established

00:07:32.085 --> 00:07:35.221 position:63%
that are White on the res
for hundreds of years.

00:07:35.288 --> 00:07:38.258 position:63%
-No way.
-Yeah, so like there's some ranches

00:07:38.325 --> 00:07:41.160 position:63%
that are on the res that are White-owned.

00:07:41.227 --> 00:07:44.264 position:63%
Is there much interracial marriages,
families?

00:07:44.331 --> 00:07:46.402 position:63%
Yeah, yeah,
there's a fair amount for sure.

00:07:46.469 --> 00:07:48.803 position:63%
-Okay. Well, thanks, man.
-Yeah.

00:07:48.870 --> 00:07:50.069 position:63%
-What's your name?
-Stetson.

00:07:50.136 --> 00:07:50.970 position:63%
-Stetson.
-Yep.

00:07:51.037 --> 00:07:53.806 position:63%
-Appreciate it. All the best.
-Nice to meet you.

00:07:58.445 --> 00:08:01.378 position:63%
Bigfoot fireworks. [chuckles]

00:08:02.082 --> 00:08:04.215 position:63%
Love it. Love the Bigfoot stuff.

00:08:04.860 --> 00:08:06.385 position:63%
An old Harley place.

00:08:07.187 --> 00:08:10.423 position:63%
Here's some youngins over here though.
Talk to these guys.

00:08:13.493 --> 00:08:14.756 position:63%
What tribe are you?

00:08:14.823 --> 00:08:20.400 position:63%
Uh, I'm Okanogan, Methow,
Entiat and Wenatchi.

00:08:20.467 --> 00:08:22.001 position:63%
-Yakama.
-And Yakama.

00:08:22.068 --> 00:08:24.268 position:63%
-Because your guys' looks
are much different.

00:08:24.335 --> 00:08:26.437 position:63%
Yeah, we had to make sure
we're not family.

00:08:26.504 --> 00:08:29.075 position:63%
-You're definitely not family.
I can tell right now.

00:08:29.142 --> 00:08:30.878 position:63%
Do you guys and the Yakama get along?

00:08:30.945 --> 00:08:33.679 position:63%
We all have to nowadays, you know?

00:08:33.746 --> 00:08:35.349 position:63%
-Who's better at basketball?

00:08:35.416 --> 00:08:38.464 position:63%
Oh… I'm not gonna go there.

00:08:38.531 --> 00:08:40.920 position:63%
-I won't say that one.
-[laughter]

00:08:40.987 --> 00:08:44.638 position:63%
Nespelem is where the agency is,
but you come to Omak,

00:08:45.060 --> 00:08:47.742 position:63%
we got the casino and everything,
you know?

00:08:47.809 --> 00:08:49.851 position:63%
So that's up there.

00:08:50.363 --> 00:08:52.398 position:63%
Where we live, it's kind of bad.

00:08:52.465 --> 00:08:55.368 position:63%
-In this area?
-Yeah, we live in an apartment area.

00:08:55.435 --> 00:08:56.969 position:63%
-It's kind of…
-Okay.

00:08:57.036 --> 00:09:00.435 position:63%
You know, you can catch it on good days,
catch it on bad days, you know?

00:09:00.502 --> 00:09:04.744 position:63%
-Gotcha. When you grew up, do you
want to stay here? Do you want to leave?

00:09:04.811 --> 00:09:09.116 position:63%
Uh… I've done both, so…
I ended up coming back, so…

00:09:09.183 --> 00:09:10.306 position:63%
-Okay.
-Yeah.

00:09:10.373 --> 00:09:12.085 position:63%
It's always been home.

00:09:12.152 --> 00:09:14.921 position:63%
We work for our family, so…
We're caretakers.

00:09:14.988 --> 00:09:17.398 position:63%
The state pays us, so that's…

00:09:17.465 --> 00:09:19.459 position:63%
-Not the res, the state?

00:09:19.526 --> 00:09:22.998 position:63%
We have to go through the state
'cause the res don't do it anymore.

00:09:23.065 --> 00:09:26.740 position:63%
So the state took over, and so…

00:09:26.807 --> 00:09:30.407 position:63%
-They treat you guys well
with the casino money, or no?

00:09:31.571 --> 00:09:33.541 position:63%
No. You don't see sh*t from there.

00:09:33.608 --> 00:09:35.893 position:63%
-You don't?
-Yeah, I don't think so.

00:09:35.960 --> 00:09:37.676 position:63%
-A lot of people don't understand.

00:09:37.743 --> 00:09:41.131 position:63%
They think it's one standard reality
for every res, but every res is different.

00:09:41.198 --> 00:09:45.413 position:63%
Some see the profits in their daily lives
and others don't, right?

00:09:45.480 --> 00:09:47.487 position:63%
Yeah. Um… I don't know.

00:09:47.554 --> 00:09:50.087 position:63%
We got that casino up there, and it's…

00:09:50.571 --> 00:09:55.828 position:63%
We've never seen our checks get bigger,
or I've never seen any change, so…

00:10:03.436 --> 00:10:07.407 position:63%
And then right across the street,
you have some nice new buildings.

00:10:07.474 --> 00:10:10.626 position:63%
Head Start program.
Don't know what that is.

00:10:11.444 --> 00:10:13.434 position:63%
Golden Eagle Senior Center.

00:10:14.234 --> 00:10:16.983 position:63%
So they're building out
some of the infrastructure.

00:10:17.050 --> 00:10:19.117 position:63%
And then this massive building.

00:10:19.879 --> 00:10:22.622 position:63%
Don't know what that is, maybe healthcare.

00:10:22.689 --> 00:10:25.858 position:63%
Yeah. Health clinic. That's what it is.

00:10:25.925 --> 00:10:29.195 position:63%
But the center of the tribe
is 30 miles that way.

00:10:29.269 --> 00:10:32.106 position:63%
We're gonna get back
out of the tribe,

00:10:32.173 --> 00:10:37.503 position:63%
and go north
to some really remote places.

00:10:37.570 --> 00:10:38.950 position:63%
[blues music]

00:10:59.592 --> 00:11:02.228 position:63%
[Peter] Sir, is this place
Tonawsket or Tonasket?

00:11:02.295 --> 00:11:03.830 position:63%
-Tonasket.
-Tonasket.

00:11:03.897 --> 00:11:04.897 position:63%
-What's your name?
-Peter.

00:11:04.964 --> 00:11:06.833 position:63%
-Peter?
-I'm making a video of the region.

00:11:06.900 --> 00:11:08.167 position:63%
-Are you?
-Are you from here?

00:11:08.234 --> 00:11:10.303 position:63%
-I am, yeah. About a thousand people here.

00:11:10.370 --> 00:11:12.373 position:63%
It's like, before we had this facelift,

00:11:12.440 --> 00:11:15.074 position:63%
it kind of looked like
the 50s type deal, you know?

00:11:15.141 --> 00:11:16.609 position:63%
-So you guys just redid all this?

00:11:16.676 --> 00:11:18.277 position:63%
-Yeah, we just redid all this last year.

00:11:18.344 --> 00:11:20.480 position:63%
There's another phase.
Actually two more phases.

00:11:20.547 --> 00:11:22.615 position:63%
Going down that way, and then that way.

00:11:22.682 --> 00:11:23.516 position:63%
It's a cool town.

00:11:23.583 --> 00:11:26.619 position:63%
-So things are going well out here?
-I think so, yeah, for the most part.

00:11:26.686 --> 00:11:28.054 position:63%
-Agriculture? What is it?

00:11:28.121 --> 00:11:29.489 position:63%
You got pretty much everything.

00:11:29.556 --> 00:11:33.259 position:63%
You got apples, pears, hay.
Pretty much everything you can imagine.

00:11:33.326 --> 00:11:35.895 position:63%
There's corn, there's…
I mean, really everything.

00:11:35.962 --> 00:11:38.131 position:63%
-Totally different Washington up here.
-Oh, yeah.

00:11:38.198 --> 00:11:40.466 position:63%
This ain't… When you think Washington,
it's like Seattle,

00:11:40.533 --> 00:11:42.627 position:63%
and this isn't Seattle at all.

00:11:42.694 --> 00:11:44.605 position:63%
-You guys feel like
you're in a different state?

00:11:44.672 --> 00:11:46.239 position:63%
Oh, yeah. 100%.

00:11:46.306 --> 00:11:48.741 position:63%
I mean, as soon as
you cross over that mountain,

00:11:48.808 --> 00:11:50.977 position:63%
you get to see
the terrain change and everything.

00:11:51.044 --> 00:11:54.511 position:63%
And then, yeah,
we're not like that over there at all.

00:11:55.048 --> 00:11:57.450 position:63%
-Good place to raise a family, safe?
-Absolutely.

00:11:57.517 --> 00:12:00.720 position:63%
Good schools, good culture,
good people around.

00:12:00.787 --> 00:12:03.491 position:63%
-So… You're from here too?
-Yeah, I was actually born here.

00:12:03.558 --> 00:12:06.025 position:63%
-You like the changes or no?
-Um, yeah.

00:12:06.092 --> 00:12:08.027 position:63%
I mean, you're gonna
keep up with modern times,

00:12:08.094 --> 00:12:09.967 position:63%
but at the same time, it's that small town

00:12:10.034 --> 00:12:12.131 position:63%
that you always hear about
or dream of, so…

00:12:12.198 --> 00:12:14.298 position:63%
-Still has that vibe?
-Absolutely.

00:12:14.365 --> 00:12:15.568 position:63%
But you know what I noticed?

00:12:15.635 --> 00:12:19.672 position:63%
You come through a day like today,
it's not too cold. The outside, right?

00:12:19.739 --> 00:12:22.508 position:63%
-Yeah.
-And you're like, "Oh, this is perfect."

00:12:22.575 --> 00:12:26.812 position:63%
And then year one, year two, or three,
most people, it's too remote.

00:12:26.879 --> 00:12:29.582 position:63%
Your closest big city,
Spokane, is three hours.

00:12:29.649 --> 00:12:33.927 position:63%
Everybody has the idea
they would love to move here to enjoy,

00:12:33.994 --> 00:12:36.289 position:63%
but the reality sets in
when winter happens.

00:12:36.363 --> 00:12:37.236 position:63%
Yeah.

00:12:37.303 --> 00:12:40.192 position:63%
It's a little more desolate up here.
We get some snow occasionally.

00:12:40.259 --> 00:12:42.660 position:63%
We hit 100, and we hit minus 10.

00:12:43.196 --> 00:12:44.697 position:63%
-Oh, that cold?
-Oh, yeah.

00:12:44.764 --> 00:12:47.200 position:63%
We are the second poorest county
in Washington State,

00:12:47.267 --> 00:12:50.254 position:63%
but we have the largest
county for square footage.

00:12:50.328 --> 00:12:53.406 position:63%
So when you're commuting
back and forth to work,

00:12:53.473 --> 00:12:57.009 position:63%
you're actually paying
high gas prices for where you live.

00:12:57.076 --> 00:12:58.945 position:63%
-Yeah, your gas is crazy out here.
-Yeah.

00:12:59.012 --> 00:13:00.379 position:63%
-$5.39?
-Yeah.

00:13:00.453 --> 00:13:05.370 position:63%
That's for regular unleaded.
I mean, and then it's $7.49 for Diesel.

00:13:06.219 --> 00:13:10.656 position:63%
And being in an agricultural area,
you're relying on the diesel.

00:13:10.723 --> 00:13:13.059 position:63%
Throw that also into
your farming equipment and all that.

00:13:13.126 --> 00:13:16.262 position:63%
So now your hay used to cost you,
say, 100 bucks a ton.

00:13:16.329 --> 00:13:20.833 position:63%
Now that bumps it up now to
375 bucks a ton or something like that.

00:13:20.900 --> 00:13:22.450 position:63%
So now your cost…

00:13:22.517 --> 00:13:25.954 position:63%
Everything's going up and these
little mom and pops little farms

00:13:26.021 --> 00:13:28.474 position:63%
can't handle it anymore, you know?

00:13:28.541 --> 00:13:30.076 position:63%
-The big conglomerates buying them up?

00:13:30.143 --> 00:13:33.613 position:63%
They definitely… Especially down
towards the central Wenatchee area.

00:13:33.680 --> 00:13:38.150 position:63%
There are larger corporations that are
coming in and buying up the smaller farms.

00:13:38.217 --> 00:13:40.922 position:63%
-Oh, man. I hate hearing that story, but…

00:13:40.989 --> 00:13:44.257 position:63%
I gotta… You know? I report what I hear.

00:13:44.331 --> 00:13:45.156 position:63%
Oh, yeah.

00:13:45.223 --> 00:13:48.061 position:63%
-It's relative wherever you go.
-Yeah, exactly. That is the story.

00:13:48.128 --> 00:13:49.895 position:63%
Midwest, here in the Northwest.

00:13:49.962 --> 00:13:52.999 position:63%
-Yeah. It's such a bummer.
It's such a bummer.

00:13:53.066 --> 00:13:55.501 position:63%
[man] The fact that we live
over here in this beautiful state,

00:13:55.568 --> 00:13:58.838 position:63%
everyone literally could vote
one way on this side,

00:13:58.905 --> 00:14:02.041 position:63%
but King County would
kind of put it null, the whole thing.

00:14:02.108 --> 00:14:04.143 position:63%
And it goes by population, so…

00:14:04.210 --> 00:14:06.078 position:63%
-King County is Seattle, right?
-Yeah, correct.

00:14:06.145 --> 00:14:08.814 position:63%
-So you guys feel like you have no say?
Is that what you're saying?

00:14:08.888 --> 00:14:09.848 position:63%
I wouldn't say that.

00:14:09.915 --> 00:14:13.452 position:63%
We have representation out here
by state representatives,

00:14:13.519 --> 00:14:17.229 position:63%
but at the same time,
I mean, it is… It's a reality.

00:14:17.687 --> 00:14:20.145 position:63%
Eh, you get heard, but not really.

00:14:20.212 --> 00:14:23.095 position:63%
-I don't think anyone's telling you
what to do out in these parts, right?

00:14:23.162 --> 00:14:26.932 position:63%
-Not for the most part.
-We're pretty self-sufficient. Yeah.

00:14:31.571 --> 00:14:33.159 position:63%
[Peter] When did you get this?

00:14:33.226 --> 00:14:35.308 position:63%
-This is my first truck.
-Your first truck?

00:14:35.375 --> 00:14:37.145 position:63%
-Yeah.
-Classic, huh?

00:14:37.844 --> 00:14:39.779 position:63%
Dude, you off-roading
the hell out of this thing?

00:14:39.846 --> 00:14:41.147 position:63%
Oh, yeah. Definitely.

00:14:41.214 --> 00:14:43.749 position:63%
I'm from Tonasket. I'm a firefighter.

00:14:43.816 --> 00:14:45.384 position:63%
-Your pops?
-Yep.

00:14:45.451 --> 00:14:46.952 position:63%
-How you doing, sir?
-How you doing?

00:14:47.019 --> 00:14:48.821 position:63%
-You did high-rises?
-Yeah.

00:14:48.888 --> 00:14:51.390 position:63%
-In Seattle, doing what?
-Concrete.

00:14:51.457 --> 00:14:53.325 position:63%
-You built those buildings?
-Yeah.

00:14:53.392 --> 00:14:54.227 position:63%
-Wow.

00:14:54.827 --> 00:14:58.506 position:63%
You know, when I retired, I came out here,
and I've been coming out here.

00:14:58.573 --> 00:14:59.932 position:63%
It's a beautiful place.

00:14:59.999 --> 00:15:02.802 position:63%
-So you came from the west side
over to the east side?

00:15:02.869 --> 00:15:04.570 position:63%
That's usually how it works.

00:15:04.637 --> 00:15:06.305 position:63%
-That's how it works?
-Yep.

00:15:06.372 --> 00:15:08.341 position:63%
-And you're loving it?
-Loving it.

00:15:08.408 --> 00:15:10.880 position:63%
-Why?
-No traffic.

00:15:10.947 --> 00:15:12.978 position:63%
-Drive around with your gun?
-Yeah.

00:15:13.045 --> 00:15:14.246 position:63%
About where you want.

00:15:14.313 --> 00:15:18.317 position:63%
Just a kickback place, so…
You know, the people are good.

00:15:18.384 --> 00:15:19.853 position:63%
Everybody's pretty outgoing.

00:15:19.920 --> 00:15:21.487 position:63%
-Right on.
-What's your name?

00:15:21.554 --> 00:15:23.089 position:63%
-Peter Santenello.
-Cody.

00:15:23.156 --> 00:15:25.825 position:63%
-Cody. And your name, sir?
-Pearl.

00:15:25.892 --> 00:15:26.959 position:63%
-Pearl?
-Yeah.

00:15:27.026 --> 00:15:28.794 position:63%
-Nice to meet you, Pearl.
-You too.

00:15:28.861 --> 00:15:30.395 position:63%
-Take care of you guys.

00:15:32.871 --> 00:15:35.257 position:63%
[engine revs]

00:15:37.637 --> 00:15:39.282 position:63%
-[man] I know who you are.
-Oh, yeah?

00:15:39.349 --> 00:15:41.949 position:63%
How's it going?
My wife and I love your videos.

00:15:42.016 --> 00:15:43.920 position:63%
-Oh, thank you. What's your name?
-Eric.

00:15:43.987 --> 00:15:45.978 position:63%
-Eric, I'm making a video out here.

00:15:46.045 --> 00:15:47.179 position:63%
-Nice.
-How is it?

00:15:47.246 --> 00:15:49.181 position:63%
-Yeah, it's wonderful.
-You're living out here?

00:15:49.248 --> 00:15:51.250 position:63%
Yep. We've been out here
for about 10 years.

00:15:51.317 --> 00:15:53.152 position:63%
-10 years. You came from Seattle?

00:15:53.219 --> 00:15:55.171 position:63%
No, no. We're from Kentucky originally.

00:15:55.238 --> 00:15:57.804 position:63%
-No way. How's it different from that?

00:15:59.358 --> 00:16:01.660 position:63%
Vastly. Yeah, it's…

00:16:01.727 --> 00:16:04.530 position:63%
We fell in love with it. It took a minute
to get used to it, you know?

00:16:04.597 --> 00:16:06.465 position:63%
It's just because it's very rugged.

00:16:06.532 --> 00:16:09.010 position:63%
But everything's so busy back east.

00:16:09.769 --> 00:16:12.625 position:63%
Just people are all over each other.

00:16:12.692 --> 00:16:14.840 position:63%
-Even in Kentucky?
-Oh, yeah.

00:16:14.907 --> 00:16:19.111 position:63%
Kentucky's a beautiful place.
But there's too many people.

00:16:19.178 --> 00:16:22.048 position:63%
Out here,
you can stretch your legs a little.

00:16:22.115 --> 00:16:24.550 position:63%
-You can see far.
-You can see far.

00:16:24.624 --> 00:16:28.873 position:63%
And once you get to know
the people here, you know,

00:16:29.513 --> 00:16:34.705 position:63%
it can be a little bit daunting coming in
'cause everybody's free-spirited.

00:16:34.772 --> 00:16:36.395 position:63%
-Okay.
-A lot of characters.

00:16:36.462 --> 00:16:38.929 position:63%
But once you start to get used to it…

00:16:40.073 --> 00:16:41.794 position:63%
-They accepted you?
-Oh, it's great.

00:16:41.861 --> 00:16:43.569 position:63%
It's a wonderful place to be.

00:16:43.636 --> 00:16:48.210 position:63%
If your thing is big box stores
and tons of restaurants, things like that,

00:16:48.277 --> 00:16:50.443 position:63%
you're probably not going to be
very comfortable here.

00:16:50.510 --> 00:16:54.246 position:63%
But if you can get into
the local thing and settle in…

00:16:54.313 --> 00:16:56.749 position:63%
-Yeah, in a town like this,
coming from the outside,

00:16:56.816 --> 00:16:59.819 position:63%
I've just seen it
'cause of what I do all over the country.

00:16:59.886 --> 00:17:05.501 position:63%
If you come in trying to push your ways
on other people, never is going to fly.

00:17:05.568 --> 00:17:10.583 position:63%
If you come in being respectful,
being cool to their culture,

00:17:10.650 --> 00:17:15.000 position:63%
asking, you know,
just coming in like slowly, right?

00:17:15.067 --> 00:17:16.535 position:63%
-Sure.
-And not pushing your ways,

00:17:16.602 --> 00:17:17.970 position:63%
then people take you in, right?

00:17:18.045 --> 00:17:21.108 position:63%
Yeah, this is one of the last places
on the planet that I've seen…

00:17:21.175 --> 00:17:22.545 position:63%
Or in this country.

00:17:22.612 --> 00:17:24.710 position:63%
-I do massage therapy as well.
-Okay.

00:17:24.777 --> 00:17:28.280 position:63%
When I first started my practice here
and I came out of a session

00:17:28.347 --> 00:17:31.383 position:63%
with one of the beloved
local original hippies here,

00:17:31.450 --> 00:17:35.656 position:63%
we were going down the hallway
and my next client was a rancher.

00:17:35.723 --> 00:17:40.446 position:63%
And they were just overjoyed
to see each other and embraced.

00:17:41.127 --> 00:17:44.196 position:63%
This is an area
where people can disagree still.

00:17:44.263 --> 00:17:47.067 position:63%
It's like it used to be,
where you can disagree

00:17:47.134 --> 00:17:49.867 position:63%
and still care for one another, you know.

00:17:49.935 --> 00:17:52.432 position:63%
[Western music]

00:18:10.423 --> 00:18:13.259 position:63%
[Peter] And we've climbed
quite a bit in elevation.

00:18:13.326 --> 00:18:15.528 position:63%
A couple thousand feet, I'd say.

00:18:15.595 --> 00:18:16.861 position:63%
What is this place?

00:18:19.340 --> 00:18:20.173 position:63%
Havillah.

00:18:21.300 --> 00:18:24.036 position:63%
A biblical name meaning Land of Gold.

00:18:24.103 --> 00:18:29.162 position:63%
Gold being the word of God, was settled
in the early 1900s by homesteaders.

00:18:33.614 --> 00:18:36.314 position:63%
Wow, this place is stunning.

00:18:36.916 --> 00:18:39.339 position:63%
This is big country.

00:18:39.406 --> 00:18:45.157 position:63%
This is like Montana big country,
but almost more remote.

00:18:45.224 --> 00:18:46.659 position:63%
It's hard to explain.

00:18:46.726 --> 00:18:49.094 position:63%
We're really getting out there now.

00:18:49.161 --> 00:18:53.421 position:63%
And I think I've seen one car.
[chuckles] That's it.

00:18:57.970 --> 00:19:00.437 position:63%
Look at that little ski lift up here.

00:19:01.474 --> 00:19:02.610 position:63%
So cool.

00:19:04.719 --> 00:19:09.390 position:63%
I love these little mom and pop
style ski resorts.

00:19:10.016 --> 00:19:13.719 position:63%
Haven't been overrun
by the corporate model.

00:19:13.786 --> 00:19:15.786 position:63%
I grew up near one in Vermont.

00:19:16.354 --> 00:19:18.554 position:63%
Mad River Glen, bigger than this.

00:19:19.291 --> 00:19:20.558 position:63%
But check this out.

00:19:21.894 --> 00:19:23.777 position:63%
It's just a one-lift place.

00:19:24.694 --> 00:19:26.244 position:63%
You got rentals here.

00:19:27.449 --> 00:19:29.649 position:63%
Oh, this looks like a lot of fun.

00:19:30.285 --> 00:19:31.485 position:63%
Just a basic lift.

00:19:33.517 --> 00:19:38.184 position:63%
Look at that lodge. I've never seen
a lodge like that for a ski resort.

00:19:39.945 --> 00:19:42.012 position:63%
Listen to the silence out here.

00:19:43.516 --> 00:19:44.943 position:63%
[silence]

00:19:47.298 --> 00:19:49.507 position:63%
[wind blowing]

00:19:50.456 --> 00:19:51.536 position:63%
Just the wind.

00:19:56.094 --> 00:19:58.336 position:63%
All right, I think this is it.

00:19:58.403 --> 00:20:00.870 position:63%
We've lost contact here on the phone.

00:20:01.424 --> 00:20:04.870 position:63%
And the dot, usually it follows,
even if you don't have reception.

00:20:04.937 --> 00:20:07.740 position:63%
But this has stayed stuck here.

00:20:08.340 --> 00:20:09.708 position:63%
And we're trying to get north.

00:20:09.775 --> 00:20:13.811 position:63%
Right up near the Canadian border
to this town, Molson.

00:20:14.311 --> 00:20:17.111 position:63%
And that's not where we're at.
I know that.

00:20:18.317 --> 00:20:19.150 position:63%
But I think…

00:20:20.286 --> 00:20:24.353 position:63%
I think we're here and I think
that's the dirt road, this one.

00:20:25.224 --> 00:20:26.224 position:63%
Primitive road.

00:20:27.059 --> 00:20:28.782 position:63%
No warning signs.

00:20:29.695 --> 00:20:32.665 position:63%
Who knew Washington
was such an adventure, huh?

00:20:41.440 --> 00:20:43.653 position:63%
Okay, which way, which way?

00:20:45.444 --> 00:20:46.444 position:63%
Okay, dead end.

00:20:47.546 --> 00:20:48.679 position:63%
Private property.

00:20:49.248 --> 00:20:50.781 position:63%
It's gotta be that way.

00:20:56.889 --> 00:20:58.063 position:63%
Okay.

00:20:58.563 --> 00:21:00.030 position:63%
That's the wrong road.

00:21:01.219 --> 00:21:02.680 position:63%
So close.

00:21:03.305 --> 00:21:04.496 position:63%
So close.

00:21:05.188 --> 00:21:07.866 position:63%
Yet so far.

00:21:07.933 --> 00:21:09.378 position:63%
The road ends here.

00:21:10.269 --> 00:21:13.072 position:63%
That's someone's house. Oh, man.

00:21:13.939 --> 00:21:16.586 position:63%
Wait, wait, wait, wait, wait.

00:21:17.777 --> 00:21:20.934 position:63%
I think I just got off course.

00:21:21.514 --> 00:21:22.581 position:63%
Is that the way?

00:21:23.949 --> 00:21:27.961 position:63%
The thing about Molson
is it really makes you work for it.

00:21:28.788 --> 00:21:30.655 position:63%
At least the way we came in.

00:21:38.100 --> 00:21:40.233 position:63%
Here we go. We're getting close.

00:21:41.066 --> 00:21:43.008 position:63%
Molson, Washington.

00:21:43.717 --> 00:21:45.258 position:63%
An old ghost town.

00:21:47.540 --> 00:21:49.637 position:63%
Oh, wow. Awesome.

00:21:50.176 --> 00:21:51.219 position:63%
What a find.

00:21:51.911 --> 00:21:52.869 position:63%
Pumped.

00:21:53.713 --> 00:21:54.546 position:63%
Yes.

00:22:00.787 --> 00:22:02.320 position:63%
What a cool ghost town.

00:22:03.455 --> 00:22:05.988 position:63%
You got the homestead cabin over here.

00:22:06.492 --> 00:22:08.494 position:63%
The site of old Molson.

00:22:08.561 --> 00:22:09.893 position:63%
Molson State Bank.

00:22:12.377 --> 00:22:14.301 position:63%
Oh, yeah. Sweet.

00:22:15.734 --> 00:22:16.601 position:63%
Look at this.

00:22:20.139 --> 00:22:21.410 position:63%
So the bank teller…

00:22:22.174 --> 00:22:23.908 position:63%
What? A hundred years ago.

00:22:24.626 --> 00:22:26.093 position:63%
Standing behind there.

00:22:27.947 --> 00:22:30.384 position:63%
Waiting to take your deposit.

00:22:31.283 --> 00:22:35.170 position:63%
Pioneers making
their riches off of mining.

00:22:36.121 --> 00:22:37.570 position:63%
I'm sure timber.

00:22:41.460 --> 00:22:43.074 position:63%
We have taxidermists.

00:22:43.729 --> 00:22:47.366 position:63%
Yeah. 1907.
It looks like that's when it took off.

00:22:47.433 --> 00:22:49.868 position:63%
1907, 1911.

00:22:49.935 --> 00:22:53.330 position:63%
These guys catching
a bunch of fish in the rivers.

00:22:54.039 --> 00:22:56.141 position:63%
And then just a lot of this.

00:22:56.208 --> 00:22:58.243 position:63%
Digging their way to wealth.

00:22:58.310 --> 00:23:00.634 position:63%
Some made it, a lot didn't.

00:23:01.780 --> 00:23:03.816 position:63%
And all the industry that came around it.

00:23:03.883 --> 00:23:06.861 position:63%
Okay, there we go, 1922.

00:23:07.586 --> 00:23:09.621 position:63%
Pretty big place back in the day.

00:23:09.688 --> 00:23:13.075 position:63%
Central Molson, lower left,
founded in 1916.

00:23:13.692 --> 00:23:15.692 position:63%
Between the new and old towns.

00:23:16.452 --> 00:23:19.765 position:63%
Its business places
were two stores, banks,

00:23:19.832 --> 00:23:22.300 position:63%
restaurant, pool hall, barbershop,

00:23:22.868 --> 00:23:25.730 position:63%
undertaker, newspaper, harness shop,

00:23:26.472 --> 00:23:27.940 position:63%
church and theater.

00:23:28.007 --> 00:23:32.244 position:63%
The last business to close
was Wilson's store.

00:23:32.311 --> 00:23:34.667 position:63%
It burned in 1956.

00:23:36.343 --> 00:23:37.783 position:63%
Look at the safe back there.

00:23:37.850 --> 00:23:38.916 position:63%
Can you go back?

00:23:40.352 --> 00:23:41.186 position:63%
Cool.

00:23:45.858 --> 00:23:49.532 position:63%
You got the old Hall's Safe Company safe.

00:23:49.599 --> 00:23:51.640 position:63%
[knob spins]

00:23:55.000 --> 00:23:56.467 position:63%
Town's money in there.

00:23:57.090 --> 00:23:59.744 position:63%
[typewriter clacks]

00:24:03.199 --> 00:24:05.410 position:63%
[cash register clacks]

00:24:05.477 --> 00:24:07.613 position:63%
The way of counting money.

00:24:07.680 --> 00:24:10.300 position:63%
Customer comes in. Gives the money.

00:24:10.916 --> 00:24:12.116 position:63%
Count it properly.

00:24:12.992 --> 00:24:14.152 position:63%
That's a tape dispenser.

00:24:14.219 --> 00:24:17.286 position:63%
And then the money
went right in the safe here.

00:24:18.891 --> 00:24:21.793 position:63%
[door creaks and slams shut]

00:24:21.884 --> 00:24:23.895 position:63%
It's got that old wooden smell.

00:24:23.962 --> 00:24:25.897 position:63%
It actually smells pretty good in here.

00:24:25.964 --> 00:24:28.964 position:63%
It's preserved quite well.
It's in good shape.

00:24:30.502 --> 00:24:32.594 position:63%
Compressor for a meat market.

00:24:37.876 --> 00:24:40.876 position:63%
All right,
let's go explore some more of this.

00:24:44.116 --> 00:24:46.383 position:63%
So cool. We're the only ones here.

00:24:49.388 --> 00:24:50.994 position:63%
Homestead cabin.

00:24:52.872 --> 00:24:54.429 position:63%
[door creaks]

00:24:55.561 --> 00:24:56.598 position:63%
There you go.

00:25:00.866 --> 00:25:05.229 position:63%
Wooden floor. Simple living.
Sewing machine in the corner.

00:25:05.836 --> 00:25:07.769 position:63%
Dining room table, dollhouse.

00:25:08.307 --> 00:25:10.578 position:63%
Severt Rise family.

00:25:19.643 --> 00:25:21.392 position:63%
[door opens]

00:25:27.960 --> 00:25:29.921 position:63%
The Poland China Mine.

00:25:33.732 --> 00:25:35.866 position:63%
It's really well kept, you guys.

00:25:36.835 --> 00:25:40.038 position:63%
Hats off to Molson.
They've done a great job here.

00:25:41.074 --> 00:25:42.557 position:63%
[door creaks]

00:25:44.662 --> 00:25:45.495 position:63%
[door slams]

00:25:48.714 --> 00:25:50.181 position:63%
Discovering Our World.

00:25:51.950 --> 00:25:53.251 position:63%
Things to do.

00:25:53.318 --> 00:25:56.021 position:63%
Get some crickets, katydids

00:25:56.088 --> 00:25:58.490 position:63%
or other insects that make sounds.

00:25:58.557 --> 00:26:01.876 position:63%
Try to find out how
each one of them makes a sound.

00:26:01.943 --> 00:26:04.730 position:63%
If you have
an old mouth organ or harmonica,

00:26:04.797 --> 00:26:07.399 position:63%
take off the cover
and play the instrument.

00:26:07.466 --> 00:26:09.701 position:63%
Which parts make the high sounds?

00:26:09.768 --> 00:26:11.770 position:63%
Which ones make the low sounds?

00:26:11.837 --> 00:26:17.142 position:63%
Say the alphabet and try to tell which
letters are made with the lips and tongue.

00:26:17.209 --> 00:26:18.209 position:63%
Wow, I love it.

00:26:18.276 --> 00:26:22.314 position:63%
If you have
an old mouth organ or harmonica.

00:26:22.381 --> 00:26:24.750 position:63%
Just like everyone just sort of had that.

00:26:24.817 --> 00:26:26.017 position:63%
Get some crickets.

00:26:29.988 --> 00:26:33.207 position:63%
This is how it was, 1947.

00:26:45.938 --> 00:26:48.643 position:63%
Look at this. They're even
showing you how to jack up a car.

00:26:48.710 --> 00:26:52.562 position:63%
How could you show that it's easier
to pull a load up an inclined plane

00:26:52.629 --> 00:26:54.296 position:63%
than lift it straight up?

