and kept an eye out for the horse thieves.

00:33:25.971 --> 00:33:28.274 position:63%
Dominion Day was
celebrated here by everyone.

00:33:28.341 --> 00:33:33.420 position:63%
Some said that boundary line did not
make much difference in those days.

00:33:34.112 --> 00:33:38.513 position:63%
But times change and bootlegging
tightened it up around 1916.

00:33:38.580 --> 00:33:42.571 position:63%
Porter Brothers lumber mill also straddled
this US-Canadian boundary.

00:33:42.638 --> 00:33:46.305 position:63%
Last to close was the post office,
September 30th, 1912.

00:33:46.892 --> 00:33:51.262 position:63%
Sidley was well liked
and settled many early day disputes.

00:33:51.329 --> 00:33:54.073 position:63%
He died here in 1922.

00:33:54.866 --> 00:33:57.803 position:63%
So I guess he had an operation right here.

00:33:57.870 --> 00:34:01.720 position:63%
And borders are always interesting places
to make money.

00:34:01.787 --> 00:34:06.559 position:63%
And there's always
a tension to borders, I find,

00:34:07.384 --> 00:34:09.216 position:63%
